.TH PHYLLO-TOKENS 1 "Phyllotaxis" "phyllo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
phyllo-tokens \- validate and inspect the installed Chroma contract
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B phyllo tokens check
.RB [ --format
.BR text | json ]
.RB [ --quiet ]
.RB [ --no-color ]
.br
.B phyllo tokens inspect
.RB [ --format
.BR text | json ]
.RB [ --quiet ]
.RB [ --no-color ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B phyllo tokens
is a read-only view over the installed package's canonical machine-readable
Chroma contract. It never derives token authority from consumer CSS, executes
project code, rewrites token values, or installs packages.
.PP
The v1 family has exactly two subcommands:
.B check
and
.BR inspect .
Unknown subcommands and unsupported options are usage errors.
.SH CHECK
.B phyllo tokens check
resolves the project and installed Phyllotaxis package using ordinary inert
project discovery, reads package metadata and the static chroma-contract.json
artifact, verifies package/artifact Chroma contract versions agree, and runs
the accepted canonical Chroma validator.
.PP
Successful text output is:
.PP
.nf
phyllo tokens check: ok (Chroma contract v1)
.fi
.SH INSPECT
.B phyllo tokens inspect
performs the same validation, then exposes the installed artifact.
With
.B --format json
the complete artifact is returned unchanged under
.BR data.contract .
Text mode is a bounded summary:
.PP
.nf
chroma-contract: 1
schema: 1
default-profile: utility
profiles: utility, editorial
roles: <count>
.fi
.PP
Consumers needing role/value data should use
.BR "--format json" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --format text|json
Select human-readable text or the common versioned JSON result. Text is the default.
.TP
.B --quiet
Suppress successful human text only. Semantic and usage diagnostics remain visible.
.TP
.B --no-color
Disable ANSI color in human output. This is also implied by non-TTY output,
NO_COLOR, or TERM=dumb.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Relevant deterministic diagnostics include:
.TP
.B phyllotaxis.package-not-found
The project resolved, but the installed package could not be located. Exit 2.
.TP
.B chroma.contract-not-found
The installed package is missing its required exported Chroma artifact. Exit 1.
.TP
.B chroma.contract-invalid-json
The required Chroma artifact cannot be parsed as JSON. Exit 1.
.TP
.B chroma.package-contract-mismatch
Package metadata and artifact contract versions disagree or metadata is absent. Exit 1.
.TP
.B chroma.*
Canonical Chroma validation diagnostics defined by the accepted inspection contract. Exit 1.
.TP
.B cli.operational-failure
An actual permission, read, or runtime failure prevented inspection. Exit 3.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Validation/inspection completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Semantic Chroma contract validation failed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage, configuration, or package discovery error.
.TP
.B 3
Operational I/O failure prevented completion.
.TP
.B 4
Unexpected internal CLI failure.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted by SIGINT where the platform/runtime uses conventional signal propagation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR phyllo (1),
.BR phyllo-check (1),
.BR phyllo-status (1)
